---
import tactileLogo from '../../../assets/CNN/Tactile_Small.png';
import highLevel from '../../../assets/CNN/High_Level.png';
import fsmSummary from '../../../assets/CNN/FSM_Summary.png';
import mathUnit from '../../../assets/CNN/Math_Unit.png';
import baselineSummary from '../../../assets/CNN/Training/Baseline_Summary.png';
import baselineConfusion from '../../../assets/CNN/Training/Baseline_Final_Confusion.png';
import dataPrep from '../../../docs/CNN/DataPrep.pdf';
import modelExploration from '../../../docs/CNN/ModelExploration.pdf';
import modelRefinement from '../../../docs/CNN/ModelRefinement.pdf';
import modelDeployment from '../../../docs/CNN/ModelDeployment.pdf';
import cnnByHand from '../../../docs/CNN/CNN_By_Hand.pdf';
import '../../styles/site.css';

const technologies = ['SystemVerilog', 'Python', 'PyTorch', 'NumPy / SciPy', 'FPGA', 'Quantization'];
const documents = [
  { title: 'The Trouble With Pickles', kind: 'Data preparation', summary: 'A look at the dataset and the practical work required to turn noisy tactile IMU readings into something a model can learn from. The document establishes the data assumptions that shape everything downstream.', href: dataPrep },
  { title: 'Architecture Search by GA', kind: 'Model exploration', summary: 'The model is treated as a constrained search space rather than a fixed guess. Candidate architectures are evaluated against both classification performance and the realities of the target hardware.', href: modelExploration },
  { title: 'Split-Model Quantization', kind: 'Model refinement', summary: 'Quantization and compression are introduced progressively, allowing the model to adjust after capacity is removed. The result is a more disciplined path toward a deployable int8 network.', href: modelRefinement },
  { title: 'The Ouroboros Core', kind: 'Model deployment', summary: 'The software model is translated into artifacts that a custom microkernel and instruction set can execute. This is where the training workflow meets the FPGA design.', href: modelDeployment },
  { title: 'By Hand', kind: 'Technical foundation', summary: 'A from-scratch treatment of the convolutional network mechanics, useful as a record of the underlying operations rather than a dependency on a high-level framework.', href: cnnByHand }
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Tactile Pattern Classification, a software and hardware co-design project by Jon Kirkpatrick." />
    <title>Tactile Pattern Classification | Jon Kirkpatrick</title>
  </head>
  <body class="case-study-page">
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Jon Kirkpatrick home">JK<span>.</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/#work">Selected work</a>
        <a href="/#about">About</a>
        <a class="nav-button" href="mailto:jon.kirkpatrick@pm.me">Get in touch</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="case-hero" aria-labelledby="case-title">
        <div class="case-hero-copy">
          <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to selected work</a>
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Software + hardware co-design</p>
          <h1 id="case-title">Tactile Pattern<br /><em>Classification</em></h1>
          <p class="case-lede">A complete path from noisy robotic IMU data and model training to FPGA-ready, quantized inference artifacts.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/JonKirkpatrick/tactile-classification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#documents">Browse abstracts <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-hero-mark">
          <img src={tactileLogo.src} alt="Tactile Pattern Classification project mark" />
          <span>Sense the surface.<br />Compress the model.<br />Respect the silicon.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-facts" aria-label="Project facts">
        <div><span>Role</span><strong>Research + engineering</strong></div>
        <div><span>Focus</span><strong>Edge inference</strong></div>
        <div><span>Constraint</span><strong>FPGA resources</strong></div>
        <div><span>Result</span><strong>Deployable int8 model</strong></div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
        <div class="case-section-label"><span>01</span><span>The challenge</span></div>
        <div class="case-section-body">
          <h2 id="challenge-title">A useful model has to survive contact with the hardware.</h2>
          <div class="case-two-column-copy">
            <p>The project began with a small brief and difficult data: classify tactile patterns from robotic inertial measurements in real time on an FPGA with no floating point unit.  A model that performs well in a notebook is not enough when the target is a constrained FPGA implementation.</p>
            <p>The work therefore treats software and hardware as one design problem. Data preparation, architecture search, quantization, code generation, and the execution core all have to agree about what the model is.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="architecture-band" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
        <div class="architecture-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">The design loop</p>
          <h2 id="pipeline-title">Every stage narrows the gap between an idea and an artifact.</h2>
          <p>The pipeline moves from uncertain data to a model specification, then from that specification to hardware-aware training and deployment. The constraints are part of the architecture, not a final obstacle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="architecture-diagram tactile-pipeline" aria-label="Tactile classification pipeline">
          <div class="diagram-node"><span>01</span><strong>Data</strong><small>Prepare signals</small></div>
          <div class="diagram-connector">Model spec</div>
          <div class="diagram-node"><span>02</span><strong>Train</strong><small>Search + compress</small></div>
          <div class="diagram-connector">Export</div>
          <div class="diagram-node"><span>03</span><strong>Deploy</strong><small>Execute on FPGA</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="hardware-title">
        <div class="case-section-label"><span>02</span><span>Inside the design</span></div>
        <div class="case-section-body">
          <h2 id="hardware-title">The model and the machine share a vocabulary.</h2>
          <div class="case-gallery tactile-gallery">
            <figure class="gallery-feature">
              <div class="gallery-image"><img src={highLevel.src} alt="High-level diagram of the tactile classification hardware" loading="eager" /></div>
              <figcaption><strong>One system, several layers of responsibility</strong><span>The custom microkernel, instruction set, control logic, and on-chip memory work together to execute the model without losing the structure established during training.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <div class="gallery-image"><img src={fsmSummary.src} alt="Finite state machine summary" loading="lazy" /></div>
              <figcaption><strong>Control flow made explicit</strong><span>The finite state machine orchestrates the movement of feature maps through the convolutional operation.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <div class="gallery-image"><img src={mathUnit.src} alt="Math unit design diagram" loading="lazy" /></div>
              <figcaption><strong>Parallel arithmetic</strong><span>The inference-only workload makes room for a highly parallelized math unit within the device budget.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
        <div class="evidence-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A measured compromise</p>
          <h2 id="evidence-title">The smaller model is the point.</h2>
          <p>The larger baseline reaches roughly 92% validation accuracy while revealing where the classes are difficult to separate. The deployment path keeps the model compact and hardware-realistic, accepting a controlled loss in capacity rather than ignoring the target device.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={baselineConfusion.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open confusion matrix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-image"><img src={baselineSummary.src} alt="Summary of baseline training and quantization stages" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-section documents-section" id="documents" aria-labelledby="documents-title">
        <div class="case-section-label"><span>03</span><span>Project journal</span></div>
        <div class="case-section-body">
          <h2 id="documents-title">Five documents. One continuous argument.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">These abstracts are the short version of the project journal. The original PDFs contain the full reasoning, diagrams, experiments, and implementation details.</p>
          <div class="document-grid">
            {documents.map((document, index) => (
              <article class="document-abstract">
                <span class="document-number">0{index + 1}</span>
                <p class="project-category">{document.kind}</p>
                <h3>{document.title}</h3>
                <p>{document.summary}</p>
                <a class="card-link" href={document.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read original PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-section case-outcome" aria-labelledby="outcome-title">
        <div class="case-section-label"><span>04</span><span>Outcome</span></div>
        <div class="case-section-body">
          <h2 id="outcome-title">A repeatable path to constrained inference.</h2>
          <div class="case-two-column-copy">
            <p>The project’s value is not only the final classifier. It is the workflow that connects data, model definition, optimization, and hardware execution while keeping each transition inspectable.</p>
            <p>That discipline makes the result easier to reason about and gives future models a path to the same target without starting over.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tag-list case-tags" aria-label="Tactile classification technologies">
            {technologies.map((technology) => <span>{technology}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>Jon Kirkpatrick</span>
      <span>Tactile Pattern Classification</span>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jonathan-kirkpatrick-62b428330" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/JonKirkpatrick" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
